      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The Court will hold that the full phrase in 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2710(a)(1), read with the definition of a video tape service provider and the parallel transaction verbs in \u00a7 2710(a)(4), limits VPPA consumer status to a person who rents, purchases, or subscribes to audiovisual goods or services."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The majority will adopt a categorical VPPA rule that acquiring a non-audiovisual good or service from a video tape service provider does not create consumer status, even if the person later watches free videos from that provider, while leaving the statute's other liability elements unresolved."
    }
  ],
